flowchart TB
%% The only write path, for the reader who wants to implement this part first.

%% Three authors open a pull request: me, the agent, and Renovate. They are alternatives reaching
%% the same place, not a sequence, so they are drawn side by side with no arrows between them.

%% The return path is the whole design. The agent's pull request lands in the same review queue as
%% mine, so "it wrote the fix" and "a human approved the fix" stay two events with two identities
%% attached to them.

%% The amber dashed edge is what makes this a loop rather than a line. If Flux cannot settle the
%% cluster on the merged intent, that is itself an alert — it raises one and reaches me, and the
%% only way to change the outcome is another pull request through the same gate.

  me["Me"]
  agent["Hermes"]
  renovate["Renovate"]

  pr["Pull request"]
  checks["Required checks"]
  review{"Who merges?"}
  merge["Merged to main"]
  flux["Flux reconciles"]
  done["New state"]

  me --> pr
  agent --> pr
  renovate --> pr

  pr --> checks
  checks -->|"fail"| pr
  checks -->|"pass"| review

  review -->|"a human, always"| merge
  merge --> flux
  flux --> done
  flux -.->|"fails to reconcile,<br/>raises an alert"| me

  %% Colour carries the decision and nothing else: green is the path that changes something,
  %% red is the check failing, amber is a reconcile that did not settle. The gate is blue because
  %% it is the one box that decides whether anything downstream happens at all.
  classDef ok fill:#17251d,stroke:#4f8f6a,stroke-width:2px,color:#dce9e0
  classDef bad fill:#261a1a,stroke:#bb6552,stroke-width:2px,color:#ecd8d3
  classDef warn fill:#262013,stroke:#a98a3c,stroke-width:2px,color:#ebe1c9
  classDef control fill:#121820,stroke:#71b7ff,stroke-width:2px,color:#e7edf3

  class merge,done ok
  class review control

%% linkStyle takes an index into the rendered link order, which is not the order these arrows
%% appear in the file. After re-rendering, confirm the red edge is still checks->pr and the green
%% edge is still checks->review; git diff on the SVG shows an edge changing colour.
linkStyle 4 stroke:#bb6552,stroke-width:2px
linkStyle 5 stroke:#4f8f6a,stroke-width:2px
linkStyle 9 stroke:#a98a3c